#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""am — cross-agent memory for claude-code / codex / dsh.

The store is an append-only journal plus a compiled view plus a resume brief.
Nothing here depends on a particular agent runtime: every agent can drive it
through ``bash``, so there is no per-agent plugin to write or to drift.

Layout (rooted at the directory that contains ``.agents/``)::

    .agents/
      bin/am                       this script
      config.json                  project name and defaults
      tasks/<id>.json              one record per task
      journal/<agent>-<day>.jsonl  append-only events, one file per agent per day
      leases/<id>.json             current owner and expiry
      state.md                     COMPILED from the journal -- never hand-edit
      briefs/<ts>-<for>.md         snapshots written by ``am brief --save``

Why per-agent journal files: two agents can be alive at once, and a shared
markdown file would clobber or conflict. One append-only file per agent per day
cannot conflict, and ``state.md`` is always a pure function of the journal.

Usage is documented in ``.agents/DESIGN.md``.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import functools
